\description{
\code{rf_pfn()} combines a scikit-learn tree ensemble (random forest or decision
tree) with TabPFN models at each leaf/node, as described in Müller \emph{et al}
(2025). This allows the model to benefit from both tree inductive biases and
the in-context learning abilities of TabPFN.
}
\details{
RF-PFN wraps any of the four Python classes from \code{tabpfn_extensions}:
\code{RandomForestTabPFNClassifier}, \code{RandomForestTabPFNRegressor},
\code{DecisionTreeTabPFNClassifier}, and \code{DecisionTreeTabPFNRegressor}. The
appropriate class is selected automatically based on \code{tree_type} and the
type of \code{y}. The inner TabPFN model (created from \code{control}) is passed
automatically; there is no need to create it manually.

See \code{\link[=tab_pfn]{tab_pfn()}} for details on computing requirements, license requirements,
Python installation, and data constraints.
}
